 464:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT_printf.c **** 
 465:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT_printf.c **** /*********************************************************************
 466:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT_printf.c **** *
 467:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT_printf.c **** *       SEGGER_RTT_printf
 468:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT_printf.c **** *
 469:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT_printf.c **** *  Function description
 470:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT_printf.c **** *    Stores a formatted string in SEGGER RTT control block.
 471:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT_printf.c **** *    This data is read by the host.
 472:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT_printf.c **** *
 473:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT_printf.c **** *  Parameters
 474:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT_printf.c **** *    BufferIndex  Index of "Up"-buffer to be used. (e.g. 0 for "Terminal")
 475:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT_printf.c **** *    sFormat      Pointer to format string, followed by the arguments for conversion
 476:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT_printf.c **** *
 477:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT_printf.c **** *  Return values
 478:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT_printf.c **** *    >= 0:  Number of bytes which have been stored in the "Up"-buffer.
 479:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT_printf.c **** *     < 0:  Error
 480:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT_printf.c **** *
 481:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT_printf.c **** *  Notes
 482:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT_printf.c **** *    (1) Conversion specifications have following syntax:
 483:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT_printf.c **** *          %[flags][FieldWidth][.Precision]ConversionSpecifier
 484:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT_printf.c **** *    (2) Supported flags:
 485:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT_printf.c **** *          -: Left justify within the field width
 486:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT_printf.c **** *          +: Always print sign extension for signed conversions
 487:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT_printf.c **** *          0: Pad with 0 instead of spaces. Ignored when using '-'-flag or precision
 488:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT_printf.c **** *        Supported conversion specifiers:
 489:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT_printf.c **** *          c: Print the argument as one char
 490:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT_printf.c **** *          d: Print the argument as a signed integer
 491:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT_printf.c **** *          u: Print the argument as an unsigned integer
